### Register Service Worker in Manifest

Source: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/get-started/tutorial/service-worker-events?hl=es-419

Define the background service worker in the extension's manifest file. This is required for any extension using a service worker.

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Open extension API reference",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "icons": {
    "16": "images/icon-16.png",
    "128": "images/icon-128.png"
  },
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "service-worker.js"
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Update Manifest V2 background to Manifest V3 service_worker

Source: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/to-service-workers?hl=zh-cn

Replace the "background.scripts" field with "background.service_worker" in your manifest.json. The "service_worker" field takes a single string, and the "type" field is only needed for ES modules.

```json
{
  ...
  "background": {
    "scripts": [
      "backgroundContextMenus.js",
      "backgroundOauth.js"
    ],
    "persistent": false
  },
  ...
}
```

```json
{
  ...
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "service_worker.js",
    "type": "module"
  }
  ...
}
```

--------------------------------

### Update Host Permissions for Manifest V3

Source: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/manifest

In Manifest V3, host permissions are moved to a separate 'host_permissions' field. Content script matches remain under 'content_scripts.matches'.

```json
{
  ... (Manifest V2)
  "permissions": [
    "tabs",
    "bookmarks",
    "https://www.blogger.com/"
  ],
  "optional_permissions": [
    "unlimitedStorage",
    "*://*/*"
  ]
  ...
```

```json
{
  ... (Manifest V3)
  "permissions": [
    "tabs",
    "bookmarks"
  ],
  "optional_permissions": [
    "unlimitedStorage"
  ],
  "host_permissions": [
    "https://www.blogger.com/"
  ],
  "optional_host_permissions": [
    "*://*/*"
  ]
  ...
```

