### Replace Background Context Functions with Message Passing

Source: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/api-calls

Functions that previously accessed the background page directly in Manifest V2 need to be replaced with message passing techniques in Manifest V3, as extensions now run in service workers.

```APIDOC
## Replace functions that expect a Manifest V2 background context

### Description
In Manifest V3, extension logic runs in service workers, and direct access to a background page is no longer available. Scripts in other contexts must use message passing to communicate with the service worker.

### Replaced Functions
The following functions, which were used to get a reference to the background page in Manifest V2, are deprecated:

*   `chrome.runtime.getBackgroundPage()`
*   `chrome.extension.getBackgroundPage()`
